THE MASTER CODEX OF AETHELGARD

I. COSMOLOGY, PHYSICS & THE METAPHYSICAL ENGINE

The Genesis & The Great Fracture

18,000 years ago, Aethelgard was the high Aethelian Empire, possessing total mathematical mastery over reality-stabilizing runic syntax.

During the final cosmic containment ritual, the Founders (ancestors of the 19 modern Noble Houses) betrayed the Empire's gladiator-champion, Korvan the Variable, stabbing him in the back and fleeing as the containment engine collapsed.

The catastrophic collapse fractured reality into two distinct timelines:

Objective Timeline (18,000 Years): Preserved strictly within the Mountain Ring by the hidden village of Epitaph and the true noble rulers of House Terminus via the 7-Day Perception Skip.

Perceived Timeline (12,000 Years): The recorded mortal history across the Dark Forest and the Capital; a cosmic 6,000-year blind spot was erased from mortal memory during the spatial collapse.

The Missing Gap Secret: The reality that 6,000 years of history are missing from the world is the realm's most closely guarded secret, held under absolute containment by Terminus and Epitaph.

The Spatial Grid & The 14-Day Shift

The Churn: Outside the protective perimeter of the Mountain Ring, raw geography decays continuously into non-Euclidean spatial rot.

The Fortnightly Shift: Every 14 days, all unanchored terrain, roads, and non-monolithic structures undergo coordinate rotation, re-scrambling land borders.

Continuous Respawn: Flora and biomes cannot be permanently clear-cut; their coordinates reset and regenerate every 14 days, mandating rapid cyclical gathering over clear-cutting.

The Truth Economy & Story Density

Significance and Historical Mass: Physical existence is anchored by narrative mass. High-density heroes, ancient relics, and notorious acts emit bright beacon signatures into the Churn, drawing the gaze of the cosmic Orb and the Pale Sovereign.

Sensory Voids: Disciplines like Lost Illusion Runes project purely perceptual emptiness without bending physical reality; because they expend zero causal significance, they emit zero Story Density, keeping users undetectable to reality trackers.

The Core Economic Engine: Runic Barrier Fuel

The King's Chain: Civilization survives the fortnightly Shift solely through basalt Anchor-Stone monoliths bolted into the bedrock with 50-ton iron chains.

Fuel Dependency: Anchor-Stones run on volatile Runic Barrier Fuel, not gold. Without continuous fuel infusions, Anchor-Stones fail and entire keeps vanish into the White Void during the next Shift.

The Fuel Pipeline:

Botanical Reagents: House Mire (toxic fungi and herbs) and House Widow (parasitic vine sap).

Biological Catalysts: House Blackwood (slag-weevils), House Cull (plains predators), and House Hollow (swamp-gators).

Stabilizing Binders: House Bleak (Pale Cap mushroom extract).

Master Synthesis Hub: House Shadowfen (cooks ingredients into the raw Pre-Fuel Matrix).

Safe Containment: House Gloom (encloses pre-fuel in corrosive-resistant Gloom-Glass alembics).

Final Imprinting: House Aethel (the Capital's Royal Crucible imprints final Aethelian stabilization runes).

Fuel Distribution: Finished fuel crates are distributed back to the 19 Noble Houses on a strict weekly obedience quota.

II. THE ANCIENT TRAGEDY: WENDIGOS & THE HUNT

Korvan the Variable (The Pale Sovereign)

The Uncalculated Variable: An ancient Aethelian gladiator whose erratic, instinctual combat style was the only phenomenon Aethelian predictive algorithms could never compute.

The First Wendigo: Left to rot in the bedrock during the Fracture, he endured 12,000 perceived years (18,000 objective years) of freezing starvation and spatial decay, corrupting into the Pale Sovereign.

The Macabre Communion: Retaining his predatory tactical intellect, Korvan stalks high-density commanders, subdues them, and force-feeds them a chunk of his own frozen, fungal flesh, violently mutating them into intelligent Herald Wendigos for his future assault on the Crown.

The Wendigo Evolutionary Spectrum

Minor Feral Wendigos: Regular mortals who perish from freezing and starvation in the Churn collapse spatially, rising as mindless, feral wendigos.

Vampirism (The Starvation Purgatory): When an ancient, high-density being (such as an Aethelian arcanist) endures centuries of total starvation without dying, their biology halts in a prolonged intermediate state—vampirism—before eventually deteriorating into a full Alpha Wendigo.

The Huntsman

A Bound Mantle: Not an individual entity, but a cursed spiritual office held by the last worthy mortal warrior slain by the Alpha Wendigo.

The Vow of Servitude: Bound to the Churn, the Huntsman diverts the Sovereign's endless hunger away from refugees and defenseless outposts.

The True Hunt: The Huntsman tracks the artificial Story Density fabricated by Epitaph, stalks the targeted corrupt nobles, marks them with the Spherical Idol, and feeds them directly to Korvan.

