IV. THE 19 NOBLE HOUSES OF AETHELGARD

1. House Aethel (The Crown)

Seat: The Obsidian Citadel (Ground Zero of the King's Chain).

Ruler: King Alaric, First of His Name.

Monopoly: The Royal Crucible and central Runic Barrier Fuel distribution.

The Longevity Secret: Keeps a captured proto-wendigo (Vampire Lord) chained under the citadel, starving it to prevent Alpha Wendigo ascension while bleeding it weekly for its longevity-granting vitae, blended into the Royal Spiced Wine.

2. House Terminus

Seat: World's End Gate (Surface Bastion) and The Hidden Deep Manor (True Seat).

Ruler: High Marshal Vane (Surface) and The Council of 300 (Deep Passes).

Monopoly: Border containment and reality-metric surveying.

The Schism:

Surface Vanguard: Starving frontier troops holding off Dark Forest surface horrors under Vane, kept unaware of true world history.

The 300 Guardians: Pure-blooded nobles in 18,000-year-old Aethelian armor holding subterranean mountain passes against primordial hordes, safeguarding the 6,000-year missing history gap.

3. House Crow

Seat: The Rookery (Subterranean warrens beneath Twilight Valleys).

Ruler: Master Corvus Crow (Insomniac, hyper-caffeinated spymaster).

Monopoly: The Whisper Guild (intercepted intelligence, extortion, shadow logistics).

Combat Doctrine: Operatives use gear inscribed with Aethelian Spatial-Fold Runes to execute the Shadow-Blink, short-range teleporting between shadows for decapitation strikes and sabotage.

4. House Dusken

Seat: The Velvet Keep (Duskendale).

Ruler: Baron Lysander Dusken.

Monopoly: Kinetic-silk armor and royal textile luxury.

The Silken Pact: 18,000-year coexistence with massive Gloom-Weaver spiders; Lysander reclaimed the failing house by slitting his father's throat and subduing the Brood-Mother using modified Aethelian silk-runes.

Fuel Dynamics: Sells arrow-proof kinetic silk for Capital fuel; funnels fuel to House Cull for monster-meat tithes to feed the spiders.

5. House Thorn

Seat: The Amber Keep (Thornvale).

Ruler: Marquis Silas Thorn.

Monopoly: Waxworks (lighting candles, lantern fuels, sealing waxes, royal jelly).

The Coup: Thornvale was overrun for millennia by Blood-Briars and giant Grave-Hound wasps pacified by purple alchemical smoke. Silas, an ordinary smoke-warden, shut off the smoke vents to the noble quarters to let the swarm kill the old dynasty, relit them, and seized power.

Fuel Dynamics: Exerts leverage by controlling illumination wax; purchases fungal spores from Mire and Shadowfen to brew pacifying smoke.

6. House Wraith

Seat: The Drowned Keep (Surface) and The Iron Flotilla (Deep Salvage).

Ruler: Countess Morwenna Wraith and Baron Thallos Wraith.

Monopoly: Abyssal salvage, Leviathan hides, and slow-burning abyssal oils.

Origins: The seas collapsed into the lightless Abyssal Caldera 18,000 years ago. Morwenna modernized the fleet with Grimsby iron armor and alchemical harpoons to hunt leviathans, while Thallos built pressurized Abyssal Bells to dredge lost runic relics from ocean trenches.

